The basics, as transcripts.

    tsr basics                          every category
    tsr basics -- state space           only those

One file under basics is one category. A blank line starts a new conversation,
so what one line settles stands for the next.

    a wren is a bird
    is a wren an animal? => affirm

A line with no arrow is told and not checked. `=>` checks what the brain
answered. `?>` records what it answers today where that is known to be wrong,
so a category says both what works and what is still owed: an owed line that
starts passing is reported, and one that keeps failing is not.

What follows an arrow is the reply itself where the words matter, and the name
of the verdict — affirm, deny, unsure, learn, answer, unknown, understood — where
only the judgement does.

These are not the unit tests under src. Those check one thing each against the
brain's own parts; these check that the basics still answer the way they did,
end to end, and they run in seconds. A change that breaks a basic shows up here
first.
